diagnosis_text:
A complete multi-phase diagnostic sweep of the simple_bgp topology found no fault. The eBGP session between router1 (AS 1) and router2 (AS 2) is currently in the Established state on both ends, with standard hold/keepalive timers (180 s / 60 s), 0 BGP notifications exchanged, 0 connections dropped, and exactly 1 connection established per side — consistent with a single clean session startup. The inter-router link (eth0 on both routers) is UP/LOWER_UP with 0 carrier transitions, 0 packet errors, and 0 dropped frames. Route advertisements are correct: router1 advertises 195.11.14.0/24, router2 advertises 200.1.1.0/24, each accepting the peer's prefix. End-to-end reachability between pc1 (195.11.14.2) and pc2 (200.1.1.2) shows 0% packet loss in both directions. No flap script, stress tool, or disruptive cron job was found on either router; no FRR log files record past reset events; traffic-control shows only default fq_codel queuing with no shaping or corruption rules; no ACL rules, no MAC conflicts, and no addressing anomalies were detected. The on-call engineer's claim that the eBGP session "keeps resetting every few minutes" is not supported by any mechanism or historical trace in the live lab. No device needs to be restarted; the network is operating correctly.
=== END ===